          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "Find the eccentricity of the conic represented by $x^{2}-y^{2}-4 x+4 y+16=0$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "kYk7K",
              "text": "2",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ZMUD6",
              "text": "$\\sqrt{2}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "u1xsR",
              "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "ldHOz",
              "text": "$3 \\sqrt{2}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "We have $x^{2}-y^{2}-4 x+4 y+16=0$\r\n$\\Rightarrow\\left(x^{2}-4 x\\right)-\\left(y^{2}-4 y\\right)=16$\r\n$\\Rightarrow\\left(x^{2}-4 x+4\\right)-\\left(y^{2}-4 y+4\\right)=-16$\r\n$\\Rightarrow(x-2)^{2}-(y-2)^{2}=-16$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4^{2}}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4^{2}}=1$\r\nThis is rectangular hyperbola, whose eccentricity is always $\\sqrt{2}$.",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
