              "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 3)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "The foci of hyperbola $4 x^2-9 y^2-1=0$ are",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "aoNin",
              "text": "$( \\pm \\sqrt{13}, 0)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "JPkVG",
              "text": "$\\left( \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{6}, 0\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "R3UQw",
              "text": "$\\left(0, \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\right)$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "Mcd1x",
              "text": "None of these",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given, Hyperbola $=4 x^2-9 y^2-1=0$\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{x^2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)}-\\frac{y^2}{\\left(\\frac{1}{9}\\right)}=1 \\\\\r\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{x^2}{\\frac{1}{2}^2}-\\frac{y^2}{\\frac{1}{3}^2}=1\r\n\\end{aligned}$\r\nWe know that. if hyperbola is $\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$. then Eccentricity: \r\n$e=\\sqrt{1+\\frac{b^2}{a^2}}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n& \\text {and focus } \\equiv( \\pm \\text{be}, 0)=\\left( \\pm \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{1 / 3}}{3}, 0\\right)=\\left( \\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{6}, 0\\right)\r\n\\end{aligned}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
